  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_036: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieves 0.715 accuracy, a substantial jump over RNA-only scvi_n200 (0.653) and over multimodal with resnet50 (0.632). The fusion mechanism (concat vs. weighted) is a completely untested dimension across all experiments. Config_037 is a single-variable change from the current best, isolating the effect of weighted fusion. This is informative because: (1) if weighted fusion outperforms concat, it suggests the RNA and image modalities carry differently-weighted complementary signals that benefit from learned reweighting; (2) if they are comparable, it confirms that simple concatenation is sufficient and we can focus budget on other axes (e.g., aggregation). This is the highest-information single-variable test available: it directly exploits the strongest configuration while probing an entirely unexplored design choice, making it the best use of the next experiment under a limited budget."
